  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Urban Leaders Program (GULP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is designed to address structural limitations in ODA implementation, where project outcomes are heavily influenced by the political context of partner countries and the decisions of key policymakers. To mitigate these challenges, the program focuses on strengthening the capacity of high-level officials who have direct influence over policy decisions and project execution.

The main objective is to enhance partner cities ability to solve urban challenges by sharing Seouls urban development experience and best practices, while increasing the feasibility of identifying and implementing cooperation projects. The program prioritizes the selection of senior officials with strong implementation potential and provides structured training and expert guidance to support the development of high-quality project proposals. Customized lectures and field visits are also provided to improve practical understanding and strengthen international cooperation networks.

The implementation plan consists of program design (JanFeb 2026), a preparatory course (March), the main training program (AprilJuly), and follow-up support (AugustDecember). During the main phase, participants develop project proposals and Project Concept Papers with guidance from experts and university faculty, including master planning exercises for urban problem-solving.

Follow-up activities include consulting, pre-feasibility studies, and funding linkage support to facilitate project implementation. Although there is no prior implementation record, the project is expected to enhance the effectiveness and sustainability of Seouls international development cooperation efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
